{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180058-do-we-know-who-the-members-of-the-manitou-are-yet","id":1180058,"title":"Do we know who the members of the Manitou are yet?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-27T21:16:23-08:00","id":1180058,"title":"Do we know who the members of the Manitou are yet?","content":"I know a preview hasn't been posted yet, but I'm also aware that backers have Origins, and I'm wondering if they list the gods in there, particularly the Manitou given that they are by far the most difficult pantheon to research. I'm really curious about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T21:52:13-08:00","id":1180066,"title":"","content":"Principle Members are listed in the appendix for the Manitou, so yeah!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T21:59:30-08:00","id":1180068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VioletDreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180058-do-we-know-who-the-members-of-the-manitou-are-yet?p=1180066#post1180066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Principle Members are listed in the appendix for the Manitou, so yeah!</div> </div> </div> </div>Though as a crevat, we know the names, their titles, their Callings, and their Purviews. For those who don't know what the Gods are like, it's a bit minimal, but more than enough for me to help plan a character and give look into her character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T23:00:30-08:00","id":1180074,"title":"","content":"Anyone care to list their names and maybe their titles?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T23:35:26-08:00","id":1180081,"title":"","content":"Kitchi-Manitou, the Great Mystery, Creator of All Things, People, and Manitou (note, only makes Chosen Scions, coming to them in dreams)<br /> <br /> Geezhigo-Qua, Grandmother of Us All<br /> <br /> Muzzu-Kumik-Qua, Mother Earth<br /> <br /> Winonah, First Woman<br /> <br /> Maudjee-Kawiss, the Firstborn Son<br /> <br /> Pukawiss, the Disowned<br /> <br /> Cheeby-Aub-Oozoo, Chief of the Underworld (this is that wolf god that I predicted would be included in Hero, and I was right about his Beast Purview)<br /> <br /> Nana'B'Oozoo, Prototype of Man (Wisakedjak is mentioned as one of his Mantles in this summary since there's a Purview variance)<br /> <br /> Iosheka<br /> <br /> Tawiscara","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T23:42:00-08:00","id":1180082,"title":"","content":"It's a more western take on the Pantheon and names than I expected. Winona in particular is straight up Dakota Sioux, so I wouldn't have expected her in a nominally Algonquin Pantheon. It's not lazy conflation or anything like that, just indicative of the Ojibwe lens we're looking through, which has heavy cultural exchange with the Great Plains peoples (hence the presence of Thunderbirds and Horned Serpents in their stories, which you wouldn't find with more Eastern Algonquin peoples).<br /> <br /> Even the title &quot;Great Mystery&quot; for Kitchi-Manitou, speaks to an overlap with the concept of Wakan Tanka of the Plains peoples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T10:48:58-08:00","id":1180201,"title":"","content":"Its definitely more of an Anishinaabe pantheon than general Algonquin, which is probably better, as later on down the line they could easily make sub-pantheons (or whatever their calling pantheons that share a PSP) for the Lenape, Wabanaki and other Algonquins groups. I'm interested to see why Ioskeha and Tawiscara are listed, as they are Wyandot deities that more or less could be seen as mantles of Nana'b'oozoo and Cheeby-aub-oozoo respectively, though I'm guessing that will be explained in the full Manitou writeup.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13472-~nkf~","name":"~NKF~","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T11:36:13-08:00","id":1180208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>~NKF~</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180058-do-we-know-who-the-members-of-the-manitou-are-yet?p=1180201#post1180201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its definitely more of an Anishinaabe pantheon than general Algonquin, which is probably better, as later on down the line they could easily make sub-pantheons (or whatever their calling pantheons that share a PSP) for the Lenape, Wabanaki and other Algonquins groups. I'm interested to see why Ioskeha and Tawiscara are listed, as they are Wyandot deities that more or less could be seen as mantles of Nana'b'oozoo and Cheeby-aub-oozoo respectively, though I'm guessing that will be explained in the full Manitou writeup.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good Mind and Bad Mind are in there due to the slightly greater importance of them in general Iroquois mythology - in a lot of tribes they (apparently) tend to predominate. I talked with my writer about making them mantles of Nana and Cheeby, as you said, but since Nana'b'oozoo already has Wiskadjek as an explicit mantle and the list of Gods was already small, we decided to spin off the two Gods into their own little angry cousin fight on the side of the family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T11:44:14-08:00","id":1180210,"title":"","content":"This is very interesting. I'm super glad Cheeby-Aub-Oozoo is included, he's my favorite member of the pantheon (not that I know the pantheon particularly well.)<br /> <br /> I'm surprised Kitchi-Manitou is a god, I thought for sure he'd be a Primordial, given that Brahma, for instance, is a Primordial, and he's on the same level as Shiva and Vishnu. That's not a criticism, I'm just curious as to the reason, and my knowledge of Anishinaabe mythology is fairly lacking so I could have the wrong idea.<br /> <br /> I'd definitely like to see a Wabanaki sub-pantheon down the road. There's a lot that can be done with them, but it's cool to focus on the Anishinaabe for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T12:07:42-08:00","id":1180218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180058-do-we-know-who-the-members-of-the-manitou-are-yet?p=1180210#post1180210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised Kitchi-Manitou is a god, I thought for sure he'd be a Primordial, given that Brahma, for instance, is a Primordial, and he's on the same level as Shiva and Vishnu. That's not a criticism, I'm just curious as to the reason, and my knowledge of Anishinaabe mythology is fairly lacking so I could have the wrong idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Brahma and Xi Wang Mu of the Shen both also seem to have Callings and Purviews assigned to them in the Appendix, so either their exact Status is fluctuating or they still have Scions through one means or another whilst still being Primordials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T12:27:28-08:00","id":1180222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180058-do-we-know-who-the-members-of-the-manitou-are-yet?p=1180210#post1180210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is very interesting. I'm super glad Cheeby-Aub-Oozoo is included, he's my favorite member of the pantheon (not that I know the pantheon particularly well.)<br /> <br /> I'm surprised Kitchi-Manitou is a god, I thought for sure he'd be a Primordial, given that Brahma, for instance, is a Primordial, and he's on the same level as Shiva and Vishnu. That's not a criticism, I'm just curious as to the reason, and my knowledge of Anishinaabe mythology is fairly lacking so I could have the wrong idea.<br /> <br /> I'd definitely like to see a Wabanaki sub-pantheon down the road. There's a lot that can be done with them, but it's cool to focus on the Anishinaabe for now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per Neall, there appears to be a category we might call 'Primordials who have Scions' or 'gods who'd be considered Primordials except for the fact they have Scions', of which Kitchi-Manitou is one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T12:45:49-08:00","id":1180225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180058-do-we-know-who-the-members-of-the-manitou-are-yet?p=1180210#post1180210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised Kitchi-Manitou is a god, I thought for sure he'd be a Primordial,</div> </div> </div> </div>He is! But Kitchi-Manitou is a little unique in that he'll just Create or Choose a human occasionally in a dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T13:44:18-08:00","id":1180236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180058-do-we-know-who-the-members-of-the-manitou-are-yet?p=1180208#post1180208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good Mind and Bad Mind are in there due to the slightly greater importance of them in general Iroquois mythology - in a lot of tribes they (apparently) tend to predominate. I talked with my writer about making them mantles of Nana and Cheeby, as you said, but since Nana'b'oozoo already has Wiskadjek as an explicit mantle and the list of Gods was already small, we decided to spin off the two Gods into their own little angry cousin fight on the side of the family.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Three questions!<br /> <br /> - Are any of the listed women in the Pantheon also Nokomis, grandmother of Nana-b-oozoo, presumably with Woodchucks as a specific purview in that Mantle?<br /> <br /> - Are either Nana and Cheeby OR Iosheka and Tawiscara also Glooskap and Malsum, as known to the Wabanaki?<br /> <br /> - Is Kitchi-Odjig, the Great Fisher, in the cards for the Companion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T15:13:01-08:00","id":1180259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180058-do-we-know-who-the-members-of-the-manitou-are-yet?p=1180236#post1180236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Three questions!<br /> <br /> - Are any of the listed women in the Pantheon also Nokomis, grandmother of Nana-b-oozoo, presumably with Woodchucks as a specific purview in that Mantle?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Are either Nana and Cheeby OR Iosheka and Tawiscara also Glooskap and Malsum, as known to the Wabanaki? </div> </div> </div>I am unsure, but would be willing to consult with Allen on the topic. Do you have a good argument?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Is Kitchi-Odjig, the Great Fisher, in the cards for the Companion? </div> </div> </div>I think that'd be pretty cool, wouldn't you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T15:20:29-08:00","id":1180263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180058-do-we-know-who-the-members-of-the-manitou-are-yet?p=1180259#post1180259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes and yes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I am unsure, but would be willing to consult with Allen on the topic. Do you have a good argument?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think that'd be pretty cool, wouldn't you?</div> </div> </div> </div>are <i>Jiibayaabooz </i>and Cheeby-Aub-Oozoo the same?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T17:19:40-08:00","id":1180293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180058-do-we-know-who-the-members-of-the-manitou-are-yet?p=1180259#post1180259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am unsure, but would be willing to consult with Allen on the topic. Do you have a good argument?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well they're generally equated with Nana (+Wisakedjek) and Cheeby, Malsum is even literally means &quot;wolf&quot;; but they're often more morally dualistic. Though doing some quick online research it seems some Wabanaki reject the vilification of Malsum as outside introduced (perhaps from the Iroquois?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}